{"name":"Breath of Fresh Air","hex":"#c7dbe4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breath of fresh air","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something relieving, refreshing, or new."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath_of_fresh_air"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breath of Fresh Air","blocks":[{"text":"Breath of Fresh Air is the sixteenth studio album by American rapper Gucci Mane. It was released through Atlantic and 1017 on October 17, 2023. The album features guest appearances from Lil Baby, the late Young Dolph, Li Rye, Sett, Key Glock, Mac Critter, J. Cole, Mike Will Made It, Kodak Black, DaBaby, 21 Savage, Roddy Ricch, and Nardo Wick. Production was handled by Mike Will Made It himself, J. White Did It, Zaytoven, Murda Beatz, and Tay Keith, among others. A double album that was supported by nine singles, it was released on the sixth wedding anniversary of Mane and his wife, Jamaican model Keyshia Ka'oir. Mane announced the album along with its title, cover art, and release date on June 26, 2023, and shared its tracklist in collaboration with Spotify hip hop playlist RapCaviar on October 11, 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breath_of_Fresh_Air"},{"title":"Fresh Air","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh Air is an American radio talk show broadcast on National Public Radio stations across the United States since 1987. It is produced by WHYY-FM in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, and hosted by Terry Gross and Tonya Mosley. The show is fed live weekdays at 12:00 noon ET, and some stations carry Fresh Air Weekend, a re-programming of highlights of the week's interviews. It won Peabody Awards in 1994 and 2022."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_Air"},{"title":"Atmosphere of Earth","blocks":[{"text":"The atmosphere of Earth consists of a layer of mixed gas that is retained by gravity, surrounding the Earth's surface. It contains variable quantities of suspended aerosols and particulates that create weather features such as clouds and hazes. The atmosphere serves as a protective buffer between the Earth's surface and outer space. It shields the surface from most meteoroids and ultraviolet solar radiation, reduces diurnal temperature variation – the temperature extremes between day and night – and keeps it warm through heat retention via the greenhouse effect. The atmosphere redistributes heat and moisture among different regions via air currents, and provides the chemical and climate conditions that allow life to exist and evolve on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/330px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4a/Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png/250px-Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4a/Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png/250px-Gucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGucci_Mane_-_Breath_of_Fresh_Air.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg/330px-Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg/330px-Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Terry Gross, host of the NPR radio program Fresh Air, in the WHYY studios in Philadelphia in 2004","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/500px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/1280px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/500px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" R.E.M.'s Michael Stipe has been interviewed by host Terry Gross.[citation needed]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/500px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/1280px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/500px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earth's atmosphere from space, showing a blue layer in the stratosphere above the clouds of the troposphere. The Moon is visible as a crescent in the background.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATop_of_Atmosphere.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/500px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip